### Step 1: Create the New Backend API (Java)
Instead of the old /filter endpoint with multiple optional parameters, we will create a strict endpoint that inherently joins the USERS and VOUCHER_CATEGORY tables. It will only return vouchers that are AVAILABLE and explicitly matched to the provided roleId.
**Add this to your RequestVoucherService / Controller:**
```java
    @GetMapping("/available")
    public ResponseEntity<List<Map<String, Object>>> getAvailableVouchers(@RequestParam Long roleId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                rv.ID,
                rv.VID,
                rv.DESCRIPTION,
                c.CATEGORY_NAME,
                rv.CREATED_BY AS CREATOR_ID,
                COALESCE(u.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || u.LAST_NAME, rv.CREATED_BY) AS CREATOR_NAME,
                rv.CREATED_AT
            FROM REQUEST_VOUCHER rv
            LEFT JOIN VOUCHER_CATEGORY c ON rv.CATEGORY_ID = c.ID
            LEFT JOIN USERS u ON rv.CREATED_BY = u.USER_ID
            WHERE rv.ALLOWED_ROLE = ? AND rv.STATUS = 'AVAILABLE'
            ORDER BY rv.CREATED_AT DESC
        """;
        
        List<Map<String, Object>> results = jdbcTemplate.queryForList(sql, roleId);
        return ResponseEntity.ok(results);
    }

```
